              "China’s state-run Xinhua news agency said the call on Thursday was made at the invitation of Trump.\n\nThe meeting in Buenos Aires could be a crucial turning point in the trade fight. Trump is poised to increase the tariffs on $200 billion worth of Chinese imports to 25 percent, from the current 10 percent, starting Jan. 1. He has also threatened tariffs on all remaining imports from China"
